<title>LATVIA: SKANSKA SIGNS DEAL ON RIGA OFFICES.</title>
<headline>SKANSKA SIGNS DEAL ON RIGA OFFICES.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction company Skanska has signed a deal to build a $20 million six-storey office block in the centre of the Latvian capital, Dienas Bizness newspaper said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Swedish firm signed the deal with Riga city council deputy Andris Argalis and construction is to start in the autumn, the newspaper added.</p>
<p>The target is for the first tenants to move in around Christmas 1998, the newspaper added.</p>
<p>The office block will be a mix of shops, offices and a restaurant, the newspaper added.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
